      transliteration: "Śiṟṟañ śiṟukālē vannthuṉṉai śēvitthu uṉ\npoṟṟāmarai yatiyipōṟṟum poruḷ kēḷāy\npeṟṟam mēythu uṇṇum kulatthil piṟanthu nī\nkuṟṟēval eṅkaḷaik koḷḷāmal pōkāthu\nīṟṟil valviṉai śeythālum iṟuthi iṟai\nāṟṟa aḷitthu aruḷum namphi nampāvai\nthēṟṟamām thēśuṭaiya thirumālē nāṅkaḷ vantōm\nēṟṟēlōr empāvāy",
      english: "Hear the purpose for which we come to serve you\nand praise your golden lotus feet at this small, early hour:\nyou who were born in the lineage that herds and feeds on cattle —\nyou cannot go without taking us as your servants!\nEven if we have committed heinous sins at the end,\nour Namphi, our Pāvai lord,\nwill give sufficiently and grant grace.\nO Tirumāl of certain, radiant glory — we have come!",
      tamilUrai: "சிறு வேளையில் வந்து உன்னை வழிபட்டு, உன் பொன் தாமரை திருவடிகளை துதிக்கும் காரணத்தை கேள். பசுக்களை மேய்க்கும் குலத்தில் பிறந்த நீ, நம்மை ஆட்கொள்ளாமல் போக மாட்டாய். வலிய பாவம் செய்தாலும், முடிவில் தேவன் அருளும். திருமாலே, வந்தோம்.",
      altTranslation: "Hear the purpose for which we come at this small early hour\nto serve you and praise your golden lotus feet:\nYou, born in the lineage that herds cattle and lives from them —\nyou cannot leave without taking us as your own!\nEven if terrible sins are done at the last,\nour Namphi, our Pāvai,\nwill give ample grace and redeem.\nO radiant, certain Tirumāl — we have come!",
      theme: "Unconditional Grace — the central theological declaration: the Lord, born among those who herd cattle (and thus among those who love and tend), cannot leave without taking his devotees; even great sins will be redeemed.",
      note: "This penultimate pāsuram is theologically central to Śrī Vaiṣṇavism. The phrase 'kuṟṟēval eṅkaḷaik koḷḷāmal pōkāthu' — you cannot go without making us your servants — expresses the Viśiṣṭādvaita conviction that the Lord's nature (svabhāva) is inseparable from his devotees: he needs to be served as much as they need to serve. The assurance that even final sins are redeemed by grace is a statement of prapatti (total surrender)."
